47
00:05:30.504 --> 00:05:31.105
<v Maya>Oh, that's smart.</v>

48
00:05:31.185 --> 00:05:42.854
<v Daniel>Yeah. And then there's the swarm itself, between 40 to 80 autonomous prover agents. They take on roles like orchestrator, team leads, workers, an architect, an integrator.</v>

49
00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:46.171
<v Maya>It's literally a corporate org chart running inside a</v>

50
00:05:46.211 --> 00:05:55.776
<v Daniel>server. Pretty much. And they just let this swarm run for 24 to 72 hours on a single machine, trying to generate proofs, hitting errors, fixing them, and trying again.</v>

51
00:05:56.356 --> 00:06:08.202
<v Maya>And the scale of what they produced is just staggering. I mean, five human researchers in just four weeks generated about 6.5 million lines of machine-checked lean proof.</v>

52
00:06:08.742 --> 00:06:11.023
